namespace trion:
    use formal

    section "What a verification answers":
        A verification means an examination of a specification by the trion processor.
        A verification result means the answer of a verification.
        The verdict of a verification result is consistent, inconsistent, or unknown.
        A bound means a finite limit of a verification.
        Each verification result names the bounds of the verification.

        [VERIFY-UNKNOWN]
        If a verification reaches a bound, then the trion processor shall report the verdict "unknown".

        [VERIFY-UNKNOWN-NO-SUCCESS]
        The trion processor shall not accept a specification whose verdict is "unknown".

    section "Consistency":
        A conflict means a set of contracts that no behavior satisfies in a possible situation.

        [VERIFY-CONSISTENCY]
        If a specification has a conflict, then the trion processor shall report the specification as inconsistent.

        [VERIFY-CONFLICT-NAMED]
        The trion processor shall name each statement of each conflict.

        example CONFLICT-UNDER-A-CONDITION:
            kind consistency
            input """
[D] The door is open or closed.
[A] While the door is open, the lamp shall be lit.
[B] While the door is open, the lamp shall not be lit.
"""
            expect inconsistent

        A normative sentence excludes no situation.
        A descriptive sentence excludes each situation that fails the descriptive sentence.

        example CONDITIONS-TOGETHER:
            kind consistency
            input """
[A] When a user sends a message, the API shall store the message.
[B] While the room is archived, the API shall not store the message.
"""
            expect inconsistent

        example CONDITIONS-EXCLUDED:
            kind consistency
            input """
[A] While the door is open, the fan shall run.
[B] While the alarm is active, the fan shall not run.
[C] While the door is open, the alarm is never active.
"""
            expect consistent

    section "Completeness":
        A closed attribute means an attribute that an enumeration closes.
        An open attribute means an attribute that no enumeration closes.
        A missing case means a value of a closed attribute that no statement covers.

        [VERIFY-COMPLETENESS]
        If a specification has a missing case, then the trion processor shall report the missing case.

        [VERIFY-OPEN-DOMAIN]
        Each missing case that the trion processor reports shall be a value of a closed attribute.

    section "Expected properties":
        An expected property means a relation between statements that an author expects.
        A check means a declaration that states an expected property.
        The outcome of a check is proved, refuted, or unknown.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY]
        The trion processor shall decide each check of a specification.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY-PROVED]
        If the outcome of a check is proved, then the trion processor shall accept the check.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY-REFUTED]
        If the outcome of a check is refuted, then the trion processor shall report the check as an error.

        [VERIFY-PROPERTY-UNKNOWN]
        If the outcome of a check is unknown, then the trion processor shall report the check as an error.
